WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.804
The world's challenges are changing faster
than our playbooks in every field.


00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.173
Military, business, education.


00:00:07.173 --> 00:00:09.709
The problems we face are more complex,


00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:12.712
more connected,
and less predictable than ever.


00:00:13.346 --> 00:00:18.051
Traditional methods rely on hierarchy,
doctrine, and the illusion of certainty.


00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.121
Design thinking turns that on its head.


00:00:21.121 --> 00:00:22.489
It starts with empathy.


00:00:22.489 --> 00:00:24.991
Seeing through the eyes of those affected.


00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:27.961
It thrives on collaboration,
experimentation,


00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:31.064
and the courage to fail fast
and learn faster.


00:00:31.398 --> 00:00:34.234
When leaders think this way,
they don't just find answers.


00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:36.469
They uncover the right problems to solve.


00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.905
They build solutions
that people believe in


00:00:38.905 --> 00:00:42.242
because those solutions were designed
with them, not for them.


00:00:43.043 --> 00:00:44.677
Design thinking isn't a buzzword.


00:00:44.677 --> 00:00:48.448
It's a mindset,
a discipline of curiosity and creativity.


00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:54.320
It equips leaders to adapt, innovate, and
make lasting impact wherever they serve.
